try's economic collapse the raid  came just hours before the island  nation's new president swore in a fresh  cabinet  for the first time in nearly a decade  polio has been detected in the u.s  new york health officials say an  unvaccinated adult tested positive for  the disease earlier this week but is no  longer contagious polio was one of the  most feared diseases in the late 1940s  with annual outbreaks causing thousands  of cases of paralysis many of them in  kids a mass vaccination campaign that  started in 1955 led to the u.s being  declared polio free in 1979  a judge has ruled prince harry can take  the british government to court over his  security arrangements in the uk  prince harry and his wife meghan markle  the duke and duchess of sussex lost  their publicly funded police protection  when the couple stepped down from royal  duties and moved to the u.s back in  2020. prince harry wants to pay for his  own security when his family returns to  the uk and is challenging the  government's decision not to allow that  homecoming mission ahead how some  canadian veterans banded together to  help a comrade badly injured in ukraine  at least three bodies have been  recovered from the rubble of a school in  the eastern ukrainian city of kramatorsk  local officials blame russian shelling  which also damaged more than 80  residential buildings in the area moscow  says it targeted the school because it  was being used as a base for ukrainian  troops and claims the strike killed more  than 300 soldiers neither claim has been  independently verified  a canadian badly wounded while serving  with the ukrainian armed forces is  recovering in an ottawa hospital tonight  the retired veteran who served three  decades with the canadian forces was  part of the international legion a  contingent of global troops helping to  fight russian forces in ukraine jeff  semple has his remarkable rescue story  in this global news exclusive  almost every day for two months erica  received a text message that her dear  friend jt was ok i didn't know  when he left for ukraine  if i ever would see him again in march  the 50-year-old recently retired  canadian veteran traveled to ukraine to  join the fight a couple of months later  his truck hit an anti-tank mine jt was  rushed to hospital clinging to life i  was really scared erica spent weeks  trying to arrange his rescue but was  told the canadian government couldn't  help and a private air evacuation was  too expensive so she called a lifeline  he's one of us i mean you know no no man  left behind this veteran served in the  same brigade as jt in kandahar he and  others have spent the past year rescuing  refugees from afghanistan and ukraine  then in may they learned one of their  own was in trouble jt was badly injured  in hospital close to the front line and  far from any border you've got a wounded  guy in ukraine there's no government  support available so how do you get  somebody back from a situation like that  this really was a canadian team effort  over several weeks the group of veterans  and health workers came up with a plan  jt was transferred between six different  ukrainian hospitals before finally  catching a flight out of warsaw and last  week he touched down here in toronto  it was very emotional  super amazing to get to see him again it  was an enormous  an enormous sense of relief  global news spoke to jt whose last name  were withholding by phone from his  hospital bed it's impossible for me to  not get emotional  um because  you know if i talk about alone  the amount of people that have come  forward to assist me he suffered a  broken neck fractured ribs burns a  concussion and nerve damage but  incredibly he says he doesn't regret his  decision to go  i saw families being torn apart you know  you want to get out there and help  because i have the ability to do so  it's it's one mind that doesn't find a  child  or a family or  like i'm good now on a long road to  recovery but 